# PROBE some-filler-subsumption. A ⊑ ∃r.B1, B1 ⊑ B and ∃r.B ⊑ C entail A ⊑ C: the filler is read up its hierarchy.
# construct: ObjectSomeValuesFrom
# expect: sub :A :C

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :B1 a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B1 ] .
:B1 rdfs:subClassOf :B .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :C .
